# Repo Workflow

This is **GPUCloud Store**: a marketing + lead-capture site for a GPU capacity
broker. Visitors discover GPU configs, build a cluster “plan”, and request a
quote for dedicated capacity across providers.

## Documents (different jobs)

| Artifact | Job |
|---|---|
| `README.md` | Durable product overview, stack, env, scripts (primary reference) |
| `docs/playbook.md` | Credibility / positioning playbook for the brokerage |
| `docs/SCORING.md`, `docs/cards.md` | Domain notes (scoring, card UX) |
| `PLANNING.md` | Planning & coordination — milestones, sequencing, status board |
| `OPEN_ISSUES.md` | Current open work items + acceptance criteria |
| `SCRATCHPAD.json` | Agent session snapshot (focus / next step) |
| `src/` | Implementation (Next.js App Router UI, stores, server actions) |
| `public/locales/` | `next-intl` message trees (`en-US` is source of truth) |

See the **project-state** rule for write cadences and how continuity files overlap
without replacing each other.

## Stack (orient quickly)

- **App:** Next.js 16 (App Router) + React 19 + TypeScript; routes under `src/app/[locale]/`
- **UI:** Tailwind CSS 4, Radix primitives, shadcn-style `src/components/ui/`, Motion
- **State:** Zustand (`src/stores/plan.ts`, `src/stores/ui.ts`)
- **Forms / validation:** react-hook-form + Zod; contact core under `src/core/contact/`
- **i18n:** `next-intl` + `public/locales/*`
- **Optional:** Prisma / Supabase when lead persistence is enabled
- **Local package:** `dullahan-web` (`file:../dullahanUI/packages/dullahan-web`) for page/server patterns
- **Package manager:** `pnpm` — `pnpm dev` / `build` / `check` / `typecheck`

## Divergence protocol

Never let the site and `README.md` (product intent) diverge silently. When an
implementation choice improves on or contradicts documented intent:

1. Implement it (if justified), and
2. Record the mismatch as an `OPEN_ISSUES.md` entry (and/or update `README.md` /
   `docs/*` if the user asked for a concept change). Plan any phased rollout in
   `PLANNING.md`.
